# Drafted by Gemini (R16 letter), edited.

~ arrives
Narrator: A slate-grey carrier pigeon drops from the dark onto {name}'s shoulder, smelling of wet feathers and sealing wax. Bound to its scaly leg is a tight little scroll.
theodora_mayville [neutral]: Wickermoor is overrun with crawling vermin, and the post cannot abide disorder. I suspect the abandoned mine eight hours north-west of the village.
theodora_mayville [neutral]: I dispatched a parcel rider along that road, and he has not returned. End this nuisance at its source, and this office will pay fifty gold pieces to each of you.
give theodora_letter
set skitter_letter_hook
set skitter_trail_known
if not quest.skitter_plague >= trail_of_corruption
quest skitter_plague trail_of_corruption
endif
Narrator: The bird cocks its head, watching you with one flat orange eye a moment too long before beating back into the gloom.
* Make for the mine -> END
* Hold the letter back, go home first -> END

~ theodora_pays
Narrator: Theodora sets four neat stacks of coin along the brass counter while a heavy grey pigeon shifts on her shoulder.
theodora_mayville [smile]: Fifty pieces each, counted to the penny, with my congratulations. The old workings are fit for a proper reopening at last.
theodora_mayville [sly]: A filthy business, of course, though one almost pities the surviving sisters of such wretched creatures.
gold +200
set theodora_paid
* Ask about the rider -> rider_q
* [Insight DC 14] Watch her face while we mention Stonoga -> tell_ok | tell_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ rider_q
theodora_mayville [neutral]: He was punctual, quiet, and rarely bruised the parcels. I regret the loss to the service.
Narrator: Her kidskin glove tightens on the edge of the ledger until the leather creaks.
-> END

~ tell_ok
Narrator: The pigeon on her shoulder swivels its head toward you, and Theodora smiles a moment too late, as if she had been listening for a different name.
set theodora_tell_seen
-> END

~ tell_fail
Narrator: You find nothing in her grey eyes at all, save a tidy postmistress pleased to close an untidy account.
-> END
